# Copy to `functions/.env` and fill in once the Gmail aliases are verified.
# The Firebase CLI loads `functions/.env` at deploy time and exposes these as
# process.env.* inside the deployed functions. `.env` is gitignored; this
# example file is not.
#
# LEAVE THESE UNSET UNTIL THE ALIASES ARE VERIFIED IN GMAIL.
# Gmail only sends as the authenticated account or a verified "Send mail as"
# alias, and silently rewrites or drops anything else - which is how outbound
# mail broke last time (see the comment in src/lib/mailQueue.js). Unset, every
# email keeps going out as the working address and nothing changes.
#
# Full setup steps: docs/email-senders.md

# Routine mail: monthly invoices, budget alerts, daily usage receipts.
# MAIL_SENDER=WattWise <wattwise@wattwise.site>

# Mail about something going wrong: device command failures, safety cut-offs.
# Falls back to MAIL_SENDER when unset.
# MAIL_SENDER_SUPPORT=WattWise Support <support@wattwise.site>

# Where replies go. Unset means no Reply-To header is added at all.
# MAIL_REPLY_TO=support@wattwise.site

# Where the rebuilt Firebase auth links land (src/lib/authEmails.js). Defaults to
# the production URL below when unset; override to aim a preview deployment.
# AUTH_ACTION_BASE_URL=https://www.wattwise.site/auth/action
